  "source_note": "Values are sourced from the SF32 Family comparison and quick-selection tables (hardware/chips/SF32_family.md) plus each chip's own 'Family Variants' package/memory table. Camera and AI-accelerator flags reflect only what that page explicitly states per family -- absence of a flag means it isn't documented there, not a confirmed 'no'. Package type reflects literal package-option membership per part (a family listing both QFN68 and BGA options matches both); 'QFN80' is a distinct package_types value used only by the SF32LB57xY tier, since its footprint (8 x 8 mm) and GPIO count differ from QFN68 (7 x 7 mm). Power flags: 'Li-ion' means the part has a documented 3.2-4.7V direct-battery rail; '1.8V' means the part's documented supply range goes down to ~1.71V or is a fixed 1.8V rail; '3.3V' means the part has a genuine, separately-documented externally-regulated 3.3V supply option -- NOT simply that 3.3V is numerically within a battery-input range (e.g. SF32LB523U/525U/527U run on a raw 3.2-4.7V battery rail with no 3.3V-supply variant, so they are Li-ion-only despite 3.3V sitting inside that range). Target resolution uses total pixel count as a capacity proxy, not a guarantee of exact aspect-ratio or interface compatibility -- always confirm against the target chip's own datasheet before committing a design. SF32LB52x, SF32LB55x, SF32LB56x, SF32LB57x, and SF32LB58x are split into their orderable package/memory tiers (e.g. SF32LB525U, SF32LB555V4O6/555V436/557VD3A6, SF32LB566V, SF32LB57xU/V/Y, SF32LB583V) rather than one blended family row. Where a chip page's per-tier table did not break out PSRAM/Flash by package (SF32LB57x), all tiers inherit the family-wide memory ceiling rather than a fabricated per-package number. display_interfaces omits SPI and 8080, since every catalogued part documents both and they carry no selection-relevant information; psram_max_mb is always a numeric total (used for the Minimum PSRAM filter), and psram_label additionally states the per-channel split as 'N + N MB' for the documented dual-channel/dual-pool parts (SF32LB557VD3A6, SF32LB566V, SF32LB583V, SF32LB586V, SF32LB587V) so the table doesn't imply one contiguous pool where the datasheet actually documents two independent ones. audio_dac/audio_adc/audio_pdm/audio_i2s are sourced from SF32_family.md's Audio ADC/DAC/PDM/I2S Interfaces comparison row and are uniform across every part within a family (audio capability is a whole-die feature, not something SiFli's docs vary by package or memory tier), with one confirmed exception: SF32LB55x's own per-part-number table (DS5501-SF32LB55x datasheet, 'Table 0-1: SF32LB55x Product Series') shows I2S and PDM count tied to the same HCPU+LCPU split that varies by package -- QFN68L/BGA125/BGA145 (SF32LB551/553/555, including our SF32LB555V4O6 and SF32LB555V436) each have 1x I2S + 1x PDM, while only BGA169 (SF32LB557, our SF32LB557VD3A6) has 2x I2S + 2x PDM; the two BGA145 records were corrected from the previously blended 2x/2x to the package-correct 1x/1x. The Audio filter matches on a per-dimension minimum threshold (each of DAC/ADC/PDM/I2S must be greater than or equal to the selected preset's value) rather than an exact-profile match, consistent with how the PSRAM and GPIO filters already work -- a part with more of everything than a given preset still qualifies for it, even if its exact combination isn't one of the catalogued presets itself. SF32LB52BU (external-3.3V, NOR-flash-only, no PSRAM) was added alongside the other SF32LB52x tiers from the same chip-page variant table. SF32LB55x was split into SF32LB555V4O6 (BGA145, 4MB PSRAM, 4MB NOR boot flash), SF32LB555V436 (BGA145, 8MB PSRAM, 4MB NOR boot flash), and SF32LB557VD3A6 (BGA169, 16+2MB dual-pool PSRAM, 1MB NOR boot flash), sourced from the SiFli chip model guide's per-part-number table (wiki.sifli.com/silicon, '芯片型号指南', SF32LB55x section) rather than SF32LB55x.md's own package-level GPIO table, because that source gives an explicit HCPU+LCPU GPIO count and per-part memory breakdown that SF32LB55x.md's page does not. This surfaced one real cross-document discrepancy worth flagging: SF32LB55x.md's package table states BGA169 = 119 GPIO, while the model guide's SF32LB557VD3A6-specific row gives 71 HCPU + 42 LCPU = 113 GPIO; the more specific, part-numbered source (113) was used here. The model guide's per-part table also shows display interfaces vary by package for SF32LB55x specifically -- QFN68L-package parts (not catalogued here) get QSPI/8080 only, BGA145 parts add MIPI, and JDI/Sharp-MIP support is documented only for SF32LB557VD3A6 -- so 'RGB', which appears in SF32_family.md's coarser cross-family comparison row for SF32LB55x, is omitted from all three split records pending confirmation, since neither the model guide's per-part table nor SF32LB55x.md's own Graphics feature list documents an RGB/DPI interface for this family. Max resolution for all three SF32LB55x BGA tiers (SF32LB555V4O6, SF32LB555V436, SF32LB557VD3A6) is set to 640x480 per direct confirmation from the μForge product team. audio_pdm for all SF32LB52x-family records (chips, module, and devkits) was corrected from 2x to 1x per the official SF32LB52x datasheet (DS5201-SF32LB52x, V2.5.3) -- both its 'Peripherals and I/Os' feature-bullet list ('1x PDM') and its hardware design guide independently confirm 1x, contradicting SF32_family.md's cross-family comparison table, which had incorrectly listed SF32LB52x as 2x (also corrected). This gave SF32LB52x its own distinct audio profile (1x ADC + 1x DAC + 1x PDM + 1x I2S), which did not previously exist as a preset in the Audio dropdown; a fifth preset option was added for it. audio_pdm for all SF32LB58x-family records (chips, module, and devkit) was corrected from 4x to 2x per the official SF32LB58x datasheet (DS5801-SF32LB58x, V1.8.3), which states '2x PDM' in three independent places (the headline Audio feature bullets, the I/O Peripherals bullets, and the peripheral address map, which lists exactly two PDM instances -- PDM1 and PDM2, with no third or fourth). SF32LB58x.md's own feature-bullet list had independently drifted to '4x PDM microphone inputs' (also corrected), while its hardware design guide had already correctly stated 2x throughout -- so the error was isolated to the top-line feature summaries (SF32_family.md and SF32LB58x.md), not the design-level documentation. This changed SF32LB58x's audio profile from 2x ADC + 2x DAC + 4x PDM + 3x I2S to 2x ADC + 2x DAC + 2x PDM + 3x I2S; since no other family used the old 4x-PDM profile, the existing 'audioD' dropdown preset was updated in place rather than adding a new option. free_io and ptm flags were added for FreeIO (flexible GPIO assignment) and PTM (Peripheral Task Machine, a 4-core parallel task engine for deterministic-timing peripheral offload), both sourced from hardware/chips/SF32LB57x.md's feature bullets and its dedicated 'PTM Peripheral Task Machine' subsection. A sitewide search confirmed both features are documented exclusively for SF32LB57x -- SF32LB52x.md, SF32LB55x.md, SF32LB56x.md, SF32LB58x.md, and SF32_family.md's comparison table make no mention of FreeIO for any family, and PTM appears only in SF32LB57x's own row -- so free_io and ptm are true only for the three SF32LB57xU/V/Y records and false for every other part. ai_accelerator was corrected from false to true for all three SF32LB55x records (SF32LB555V4O6, SF32LB555V436, SF32LB557VD3A6) and all SF32LB56x-family records (SF32LB566V, SF32LB567V, SF32LB56-MOD, SF32LB56-DevKit-LCD), per each chip's own 'Graphics, Display, and AI' section, which documents a 'Neural-network matrix accelerator for TinyML workloads' for both families (1.92GOPS/5.73TOPS/W for 55x, 1.92GOPS/>10TOPS/W for 56x) -- SF32_family.md's coarser comparison table doesn't call this out per-family the way the individual chip pages do, which is why it had been missed originally. SF32LB52x.md and SF32LB57x.md document no equivalent accelerator, so those families remain ai_accelerator: false. wifi (external Wi-Fi via SDIO) was corrected from false to true for SF32LB52BU and for all three SF32LB55x records (SF32LB555V4O6, SF32LB555V436, SF32LB557VD3A6) and all three SF32LB57x records (SF32LB57xU/V/Y), per direct confirmation from the μForge product team -- unlike SF32LB56x and SF32LB58x, whose own chip pages explicitly state 'External Wi-Fi connectivity through SDIO', SF32LB52x.md, SF32LB55x.md, and SF32LB57x.md don't spell this out per-part, so this correction relies on the product team's direct confirmation rather than a chip-page citation; the other SF32LB52x tiers (523U/525U/527U/52JU/52DU) were not included in this correction and remain wifi: false pending the same confirmation.",
